course: dictionary
lesson: 10259
title: Tonsils and germs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your tonsils are two small, soft lumps at the back of your throat, one on each side. They help your body fight germs. «Tonsils are lumps at the back of the throat that help fight germs.» So a tonsil is part of your body's defence system.
explain: Sometimes tonsils get infected and swollen. Doctors call this tonsillitis, and your throat hurts when it happens. «A few bouts of tonsillitis (sore, swollen tonsils) are not a reason to take them out.» The brackets tell you the meaning, so you can read the rest of the sentence without getting stuck.
explain: Some children have their tonsils taken out in an operation. This is called a tonsillectomy. Fewer tonsil operations are done now than in the past, so do not assume every sore throat means an operation.
explain: Most sore throats are caused by viruses and get better within about a week. Some are caused by streptococcus bacteria. Germs can be viruses or bacteria, and both can make your throat sore.
fact: Tonsils are two small, soft lumps at the back of your throat.
fact: Tonsils help fight germs, so they are part of the immune system.
fact: Tonsillitis means your tonsils are infected and swollen, and your throat hurts.
fact: A tonsillectomy is an operation to take the tonsils out.
fact: Most sore throats are caused by viruses and get better within about a week.
exercise: What do tonsils do? | *They help fight germs | They help you digest food | They make your voice louder | They pump blood round the body
exercise: «Most sore throats are caused by viruses and get better within about a week.» What does this tell you? | Sore throats never get better | Sore throats only happen to adults | *Most sore throats clear up on their own in about a week | Sore throats always need an operation
exercise: Find the word in «a few bouts of tonsillitis (sore, swollen tonsils)» that means sore, swollen tonsils. | tonsils | *tonsillitis | operations | viruses
test: Where are your tonsils? | *At the back of your throat, one on each side | Inside your ears | In your stomach | On your ankles
test: «Fewer tonsil operations are done now than in the past.» What does operation mean here? | A piece of music | A type of sport | A simple sum | *An operation, such as taking tonsils out, done by doctors
exam: Which word means an operation to take the tonsils out? | Immune | Tonsillitis | Virus | *Tonsillectomy
